      "concept": "Syllogism",
      "confidence": "high",
      "marks_pos": 1.0,
      "marks_neg": 0.25,
      "question": "Two statements are given followed by two conclusions numbered I and II. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follow(s) from the statements.\n\n**Statements:**\n\nAll hens are dogs.\n\nAll dogs are peacocks.\n\n**Conclusions:**\n\nI. All hens are peacocks.\n\nII. All peacocks are dogs.",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "Only conclusion II follows"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "Only conclusion I follows"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "Neither conclusion I nor II follows"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "Both conclusions I and II follow"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "2",
      "solution": "Given Statements:\n\nAll hens are dogs.\n\nAll dogs are peacocks.\n\nThe least possible Venn diagram is as follows:\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2bd435259b801b826dcf10381132da31cff4cace843e05f08abf0220547347b5.png] [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/086f25ccdd857fb428cacd80b3a2719c029f51d09a7e76ccc2b923d6d222b4c5.png] \n\nConclusions:\n\nI. All hens are peacocks. - **True **(because All hens are dogs and All dogs are peacocks. So, All hens are peacocks too)\n\nII. All peacocks are dogs. - **False **(because All dogs are peacocks given. So, All peacocks are dogs it is not definite)\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"Only conclusion I follows\".**",
      "solution_images": [
        {
          "url": "https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2bd435259b801b826dcf10381132da31cff4cace843e05f08abf0220547347b5.png",
