      "confidence": "high",
      "marks_pos": 1.0,
      "marks_neg": 0.25,
      "question": "Select the set in which the numbers are NOT related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets.\n\n(59, 236, 175),(24, 124, 98)\n\n(NOTE: Operations should be performed on the whole numbers, without breaking down the numbers into its constituent digits.)",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "(22, 183, 159)"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "(21, 124, 108)"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "(64, 182, 116)"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "(16, 206, 188)"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "2",
      "solution": "The logic followed here is: **(1st number + 3rd number) + 2 = 2nd number.**\n\n(59, 236, 175) → (59 + 175) + 2 = 234 + 2 = **236 (2nd number)**\n\n(24, 124, 98) → (24 + 98) + 2 = 122 + 2 = **124 **(2nd number)\n\nOption 1) (22, 183, 159) → (22 + 159) + 2 = 181 + 2 = 183\n\n**Option 2) (21, 124, 108) → (21 + 108) + 2 = 129 + 2 = 131 ≠ 124**\n\nOption 3) (64, 182, 116) → (64 + 116) + 2 = 180 + 2 = 182\n\nOption 4) (16, 206, 188) → (16 + 188) + 2 = 204 + 2 = 206\n\nSo, the numbers (21, 124, 108) are NOT related in the same way as are the numbers of the following sets.\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"(21, 124, 108)\".**",
      "tags": [
        "Letter and Number Based"
      ]
    },
